{
  "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
  "id": "boss-ce1",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Boss CE-1 Chorus Ensemble (Roland ET-10C, MN3002)",
  "description": "Roland / Boss CE-1 Chorus Ensemble (model ET-10C, 1976), traced directly from the factory Roland ET-10C schematic including PCB wire-pad numbering, factory 440 Hz test-point oscillograms (A-N), and the Roland service note for IC-4 Schmitt thresholds (R80 = 120 kOhm, R81 = 150 kOhm for uPC1458). Mains-fed +-14 V tracking regulator (18 VAC CT -> D16-D19 1N4001 bridge -> C46/C47 220 uF -> Q17 2SB434 zener-referenced -14 V pass + Q16 2SC900 sense + Q15 2SD234 +14 V tracking pass -> R10/C4, R17/C10 +-13 V preamp rails). Input section: S1 HIGH/LOW sensitivity switch (LOW direct to VR11 50 kA Level Control; HIGH through Q1 2SC900 mic amp, 20 dB) -> IC-1 TA7136P non-inverting preamp (1 + 470k/10k = +33.6 dB) -> R13/C08/R15 pre-emphasis + R14/R16/C12/C11/Q2 3-pole Sallen-Key anti-aliasing filter -> IC-2 Panasonic MN3002 512-stage PMOS BBD (+4.41 V VBB substrate, -3.45 V VBias, -13.0 V VGG, -14 V VDD, 100 kOhm drain loads R24/R25 + VR01 5 kB clock-null trim) -> Q7 emitter follower -> R41/C26 de-emphasis + R42/R43/R44/C28/C29/C27/Q10 3-pole Sallen-Key reconstruction filter -> Q12 2SK30A shunt noise-killer JFET driven by IC-3 TA7136P (+43.1 dB) + D11/D12/C41/C42/D10 envelope detector -> Q13 2SK30A wet FET switch -> passive Dry (R47/C31/R49/R52/R51/R91) + Wet (R48/R90/R54/R92) mono-normalled output mixer. Dual-mode LFO (IC-4 uPC1458): Chorus mode (S4 = 0) runs IC-4A/B as a variable-rate Schmitt/integrator triangle LFO (0.40-3.05 Hz via VR12 10 kB Intensity); Vibrato mode (S4 = 1) reconfigures IC-4B into a 3-pole diode-AGC phase-shift sine oscillator (3.7-13.4 Hz via VR14 100 kC Rate, attenuated by VR13 50 kB Depth). Discrete Q3-Q6 (2SA493/2SC536F) clamped astable VCO (57-400 kHz, above audio Nyquist) fitted from a 21-point ngspice characterisation with D03/D04 clamping pump.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Roland Corporation, 'BOSS Chorus Ensemble Model CE-1 Schematic Diagram' (drawing ET-10C, 1976: full circuit, PCB pad numbers, DC voltages and 440 Hz square-wave oscillograms A-N)",
      "url": "https://archive.org/details/CE-1_SCHEMATICS"
    },
    {
      "title": "Roland / Boss CE-1 Service Notes (IC-4 table: R80 = 120 kOhm, R81 = 150 kOhm required for NEC uPC1458; VR01 BBD balance procedure)",
      "url": "https://archive.org/details/CE-1_SCHEMATICS"
    },
    {
      "title": "Panasonic MN3002 512-stage PMOS Bucket Brigade Device specification (512 stages, VBB/VDD/VGG bias, 0.4% THD, 70 dB S/N)",
      "url": "work/circuit-netlists/wave-c/DEVICES.md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Toshiba TA7136P Low-Noise Preamplifier IC datasheet (Av0 = 90 dB typ, ICC = 0.85 mA typ, pin 2 = +IN, pin 3 = -IN, external lag compensation)",
      "url": "https://datasheetspdf.com/pdf-file/530285/Toshiba/TA7136P/1"
    },
    {
      "title": "NEC uPC1458C / TI MC1458 Dual Operational Amplifier datasheet (Av = 200 V/mV typ, GBW = 1 MHz, SR = 0.5 V/us, Vos = 1-5 mV)",
      "url": "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/mc1458.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Toshiba 2SK30ATM N-channel JFET datasheet (GR rank: IDSS 2.6-6.5 mA, VGS(off) -0.4 to -5.0 V)",
      "url": "https://toshiba.semicon-storage.com/info/2SK30ATM_datasheet_en_20140301.pdf?did=19684"
    }
  ],
